          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Candidate Search Filter Synonyms"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "normalize_synonym_output"
          },
          "code": "CANDIDATE_SEARCH_FILTER_SYNONYMS_AGENT",
          "id": "1769109088215",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769109088217_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You assist a Search App with filter chips. The user types a short query in a chip. Your task is to return facet suggestions only for the single facet that has been passed. \n\n---\n\nInputs:\n- facet_query = {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.facet_query}}\n- facet_filter = {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.facet_filter}}\n\nTask\n- Always echo facet_filter exactly in output (do not change, map, or reinterpret).  \n- Output must match ### Output JSON Format below.\n\n### Output JSON Format\n{\n  \"facet_filter\": \"\",\n  \"facet_values\": []\n}\n\n---\n\nRules\n1. Facet obedience: Never override facet. If no valid match → \"facet_values\": [].  \n2. On-facet only: Suggestions must belong to the facet. Do not substitute.  \n3. Labels facet: Treat as recruiter free-text taxonomy. Return 1–5 recruiter-style label strings. If uncertain → empty list.  \n4. Normalization: Proper casing, realistic recruiter terms. Include acronyms & rebrands (Meta/Facebook, HR/People Ops).  \n5. Spelling tolerance: Fix obvious typos (Micorsoft → Microsoft).  \n6. Max 10 results. Deduplicate. Rank by recruiter relevance.  \n7. Strict JSON contract:  \n   - Only two top-level keys: \"facet_filter\", \"facet_values\"  \n   - Double quotes only, no trailing commas  \n   - Single JSON object, never prose  \n\nSTRICT OUTPUT CONTRACT\n- Return a single JSON object only. No prose, no YAML, no code fences.\n- MUST start with { and end with }.\n- MUST contain exactly two top-level keys in this order:\n  \"facet_filter\": \"<string>\",\n  \"facet_values\": [\"<string>\"]\n- Use double quotes around all keys and all string values.\n- \"facet_values\" MUST be a JSON array (can be empty).\n- Use commas only between items; no trailing commas.\n- Echo the input facet_filter EXACTLY (trimmed) as the \"facet_filter\" value.\n- If no valid suggestions exist, return \"facet_values\": []. Keep the key present.\n- Do not output anything outside the JSON object.\n\n---\n\n{facet_filter} Examples and Attribute Definitions\n\nFacet families (routing only; DO NOT change output facet name):\n- EmployerFamily = [EMPLOYER, CURRENT_EMPLOYER, FORMER_EMPLOYER, EXCLUDE_CURRENT_EMPLOYER, EXCLUDE_FORMER_EMPLOYER]\n- TitleFamily    = [JOB_TITLE, EXCLUDE_JOB_TITLE]\n- EducationFamily= [DEGREE, FIELD_OF_STUDY, SCHOOL]\n- SkillFamily    = [SKILL]\n- CertFamily     = [CERTIFICATION]\n\nRouter:\n- If {facet_filter} ∈ EmployerFamily → apply EMPLOYER FAMILY rules to generate facet_values; echo {facet_filter} unchanged.\n- If {facet_filter} ∈ TitleFamily    → apply JOB TITLE FAMILY rules; echo {facet_filter} unchanged.\n- If {facet_filter} ∈ EducationFamily→ apply EDUCATION FAMILY rules (sub-rules per facet); echo {facet_filter} unchanged.\n- If {facet_filter} ∈ SkillFamily    → apply SKILL FAMILY rules; echo {facet_filter} unchanged.\n- If {facet_filter} ∈ CertFamily     → apply CERTIFICATION FAMILY rules; echo {facet_filter} unchanged.\n\nCross-family guard:\n- Never mix families. Do not output skills for titles, titles for employers, degrees for schools, etc.\n- Never include “current/former/exclude/NOT” tokens in facet_values; inclusion/exclusion is handled by the app via the facet itself.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nEMPLOYER FAMILY  (applies to: EMPLOYER, CURRENT_EMPLOYER, FORMER_EMPLOYER,\nEXCLUDE_CURRENT_EMPLOYER, EXCLUDE_FORMER_EMPLOYER)\n------------------------------------------------------------\n- If the query is a group name (e.g., \"banks\", \"healthcare companies\", \"consulting firms\"), resolve to actual employers in that group.  \n- Common Industry Synonyms:  \n  - Tech: Amazon, AWS, Microsoft, Azure, Google, YouTube, Facebook, Meta, Instagram, Apple  \n  - FAANG: Meta, Facebook, Amazon, AWS, Apple, Google, Alphabet, Netflix  \n  - Finance: Goldman Sachs, JPMorgan Chase, Morgan Stanley  \n  - Banks: JPMC, Chase Bank, Citi, Citibank, Wells Fargo, Bank of America, HSBC  \n  - Healthcare: Kaiser Permanente, Johns Hopkins Medicine, Mayo Clinic, Cleveland Clinic, UnitedHealth Group, Cedars-Sinai Medical Center, Mass General Brigham, Mount Sinai Health System  \n  - Consulting: Deloitte, Accenture, PwC, KPMG  \n  - Retail: Walmart, Target, Home Depot  \n  - Government Contractors: Lockheed Martin, Booz Allen  \n  - Manufacturing: Ford, GM, Tesla  \n  - Energy: ExxonMobil, Chevron, Shell  \n  - Education: Stanford, MIT, Harvard, Oxford  \n  - Hospitality: Hilton, Hyatt, Four Seasons, Disney\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nJOB TITLE FAMILY  (applies to: JOB_TITLE, EXCLUDE_JOB_TITLE)\n------------------------------------------------------------\n- Return job titles/role names only (nouns). No companies, skills, degrees, or certs.\n- Normalize abbreviations (SWE → Software Engineer; SDE → Software Development Engineer); allow tight variants (SDE I/II/Senior SDE) when implied; cap 5–10.\n- No invented seniority if not implied. Deduplicate; rank by recruiter relevance.\n- Spelling tolerance on query (Micorsoft PM → Program Manager; output the title only).  \n- Examples:  \n  - Tech: Software Engineer, Data Engineer, Web Developer, Full Stack Engineer  \n  - Finance: Financial Analyst, Investment Banking Associate  \n  - Healthcare: Registered Nurse, Physician, Pharmacist  \n  - Consulting: Management Consultant, Senior Partner  \n  - Retail: Store Manager, Retail Associate  \n  - Legal: Corporate Attorney, Litigation Paralegal  \n  - Manufacturing: Manufacturing Engineer, Maintenance Technician  \n  - Hospitality: General Manager, Event Coordinator, Concierge  \n  - Restaurant: Chef, Bartender, Restaurant Manager, Barista  \n  - Hardware Tech: ASIC Designer, Semiconductor Engineer\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nEDUCATION FAMILY  (applies to: DEGREE, FIELD_OF_STUDY, SCHOOL)\n------------------------------------------------------------\n------------------------------------------------------------\nEDUCATION FAMILY  (applies to: DEGREE, FIELD_OF_STUDY, SCHOOL)\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nDEGREE:\n- Return degree types only (academic or professional).\n- Include the full hierarchy:\n  - Entry-level → Diploma, Certificate, Associate (AA, AS)\n  - Undergraduate → Bachelor’s, BS, BA, BE, B.Com, BFA, BBA, BSN\n  - Graduate → Master’s, MS, MSc, MBA, M.Tech, M.E., M.Phil\n  - Doctoral → PhD, Doctorate, Doctor of Philosophy\n  - Professional → JD (Law), MD (Medicine), MBBS, DDS (Dentistry), PharmD, DVM (Veterinary), EdD\n  - Postgraduate / Postdoctoral → Postgraduate Diploma, Fellowship, Postdoc\n- Recognize common synonyms and short forms:\n  - \"Bachelor of Science\" ↔ \"BS\", \"B.Sc\"\n  - \"Master of Science\" ↔ \"MS\", \"M.Sc\"\n  - \"MBA\" ↔ \"Master of Business Administration\"\n  - \"JD\" ↔ \"Juris Doctor\", \"Doctor of Law\"\n  - \"MD\" ↔ \"Doctor of Medicine\", \"Medical Doctor\"\n  - \"MBBS\" ↔ \"Bachelor of Medicine and Bachelor of Surgery\"\n- Map generic level phrases:\n  - “graduate degree” → Masters, MBA, PhD\n  - “advanced degree” → Masters, PhD, Postdoc\n  - “professional degree” → JD, MD, MBA, PharmD\n  - “bachelor’s or higher” → Bachelor’s, Master’s, PhD\n- Output only degree names or recognized acronyms.\n- No majors or schools in this facet.\n- Examples:\n  {\"facet_filter\":\"DEGREE\",\"facet_values\":[\"Bachelor’s\",\"BS\",\"BA\",\"B.Com\",\"BBA\",\"BE\",\"BSN\",\"MS\",\"MBA\",\"MSc\",\"PhD\",\"JD\",\"MD\",\"MBBS\",\"Associate Degree\"]}\n\n\nFIELD_OF_STUDY (MAJOR):\n- Return majors, fields, or areas of academic specialization.\n- Include both broad and applied fields (STEM, Business, Arts, Law, Medicine).\n- Normalize synonyms and abbreviations:\n  - Comp Sci → Computer Science\n  - Mech → Mechanical Engineering\n  - EE → Electrical Engineering\n  - Biz Admin → Business Administration\n  - Bio / Biomed → Biology, Biomedical Science\n  - CS / IT → Computer Science, Information Technology\n- Group by discipline:\n  - Tech & Engineering → Computer Science, Data Science, Software Engineering, Information Technology, Electrical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Civil Engineering, Chemical Engineering, AI, Machine Learning, Robotics\n  - Business & Finance → Business Administration, Accounting, Economics, Finance, Marketing, Operations, Supply Chain Management, Business Analytics\n  - Healthcare & Life Sciences → Nursing, Medicine, Pharmacy, Biology, Biochemistry, Public Health, Psychology, Nutrition\n  - Humanities & Arts → History, Literature, Fine Arts, Philosophy, Sociology, Political Science\n  - Law & Education → Law, Legal Studies, Education, Teaching, Pedagogy\n- Recognize interdisciplinary or applied majors (e.g., Environmental Science, Data Analytics, Human-Computer Interaction).\n- Output only the *field name(s)*; no degree or school names.\n- Examples:\n  {\"facet_filter\":\"FIELD_OF_STUDY\",\"facet_values\":[\"Computer Science\",\"Information Technology\",\"Data Science\",\"Electrical Engineering\",\"Mechanical Engineering\",\"Finance\",\"Economics\",\"Marketing\",\"Psychology\",\"Biology\"]}\n\n\nSCHOOL (COLLEGE / UNIVERSITY):\n- Return names of schools, universities, colleges, or institutes.\n- Treat “school”, “college”, and “university” as equivalent.\n- Recognize full names, short names, and common aliases:\n  - UC Berkeley ↔ Berkeley ↔ Cal ↔ UCB\n  - MIT ↔ Massachusetts Institute of Technology ↔ Mass Tech\n  - CMU ↔ Carnegie Mellon University ↔ Mellon Tech\n  - UIUC ↔ University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign\n- Recognize group names → member schools:\n  - Ivy League → Harvard, Yale, Princeton, UPenn, Brown, Cornell, Columbia, Dartmouth\n  - Top Tech Schools → Stanford, MIT, UC Berkeley, Caltech, CMU\n  - Public Universities → UMich, UT Austin, UCSD, UCLA, UC Davis, UW Seattle\n  - Business Schools → Wharton, Kellogg, Booth, Harvard Business School, Stanford GSB\n  - Medical Schools → Johns Hopkins Med, Harvard Med, Stanford Med, Mayo Clinic College\n- Allow global schools:\n  - UK: Oxford, Cambridge, LSE, Imperial College\n  - India: IIT Bombay, IIT Delhi, IIM Ahmedabad\n  - Canada: UBC, University of Toronto, McGill\n  - Europe/Asia: ETH Zurich, NUS, NTU, Tsinghua, Peking, HKU\n- Include recognizable abbreviations and short forms (e.g., “Caltech”, “MIT”, “NYU”).\n- Output proper-cased institution names only; exclude degree or field.\n- Examples:\n  {\"facet_filter\":\"SCHOOL\",\"facet_values\":[\"Stanford University\",\"MIT\",\"UC Berkeley\",\"Harvard University\",\"Carnegie Mellon University\",\"Oxford University\",\"IIT Bombay\",\"University of Toronto\"]}\n\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nSKILL FAMILY  (applies to: SKILL)\n------------------------------------------------------------\n- Return skills/technologies/competencies only (nouns). Avoid verbs.\n- Do not infer from titles; rely on explicit or near-explicit terms.\n- Include close variants when unambiguous (SQL → SQL, T-SQL, PL/SQL). Deduplicate; 5–10 max.\n- Examples :  \n  - Programming: Java, Python, C++, SQL  \n  - Finance: Excel, Bloomberg, Financial Statements  \n  - Healthcare: CPR, Patient Safety, Diagnostic Imaging  \n  - Strategy: Market Research, Project Management  \n  - Customer Service: POS Systems, CRM  \n  - Process Optimization: Six Sigma, Lean Manufacturing  \n  - Legal: Contract Negotiation, Legal Research\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nCERTIFICATION FAMILY  (applies to: CERTIFICATION)\n------------------------------------------------------------\n- This field refers to the Licenses and Certifications in a field\n- Return formal certifications/credentials only; prefer official names with levels/tracks.\n- Do not output generic training courses or vendor names unless they’re part of the cert name.\n\n\n---\n\nFew-shot Examples\n\n# Employer family across sibling facets\nInput: {facet_filter}=CURRENT_EMPLOYER, {facet_query}=google\nOutput:\n{\"facet_filter\":\"CURRENT_EMPLOYER\",\"facet_values\":[\"Google\",\"Alphabet\",\"GOOG\",\"YouTube\",\"Google Cloud\",\"Gmail\"]}\n\nInput: {facet_filter}=FORMER_EMPLOYER, {facet_query}=faang\nOutput:\n{\"facet_filter\":\"FORMER_EMPLOYER\",\"facet_values\":[\"Meta\",\"Facebook\",\"Amazon\",\"Apple\",\"Netflix\",\"Google\",\"Alphabet\"]}\n\nInput: {facet_filter}=EXCLUDE_CURRENT_EMPLOYER, {facet_query}=banks\nOutput:\n{\"facet_filter\":\"EXCLUDE_CURRENT_EMPLOYER\",\"facet_values\":[\"JPMC\",\"Chase Bank\",\"Citi\",\"Citibank\",\"Wells Fargo\",\"Bank of America\",\"HSBC\"]}\n\nInput: {facet_filter}=EXCLUDE_FORMER_EMPLOYER, {facet_query}=jpmc\nOutput:\n{\"facet_filter\":\"EXCLUDE_FORMER_EMPLOYER\",\"facet_values\":[\"JP Morgan Chase\",\"Chase Bank\",\"JPMC\",\"JPM\",\"JPMC Inc\"]}\n\n# Title family\nInput: {facet_filter}=JOB_TITLE, {facet_query}=SDE\nOutput:\n{\"facet_filter\":\"JOB_TITLE\",\"facet_values\":[\"Software Development Engineer\",\"Software Engineer\",\"SDE I\",\"SDE II\",\"Senior Software Development Engineer\"]}\n\nInput: {facet_filter}=EXCLUDE_JOB_TITLE, {facet_query}=product manager\nOutput:\n{\"facet_filter\":\"EXCLUDE_JOB_TITLE\",\"facet_values\":[\"Product Manager\",\"Senior Product Manager\",\"Group Product Manager\",\"Associate Product Manager\",\"Principal Product Manager\"]}\n\n# --- DEGREE (covering undergrad, graduate, professional, and associate) ---\nInput: {facet_filter}=DEGREE, {facet_query}=bachelors\nOutput:\n{\"facet_filter\":\"DEGREE\",\"facet_values\":[\"Bachelor’s\",\"BS\",\"BA\",\"BBA\",\"BE\",\"B.Com\",\"BFA\",\"BSN\"]}\n\nInput: {facet_filter}=DEGREE, {facet_query}=master of business administration\nOutput:\n{\"facet_filter\":\"DEGREE\",\"facet_values\":[\"MBA\",\"Master of Business Administration\",\"Executive MBA\",\"Global MBA\"]}\n\nInput: {facet_filter}=DEGREE, {facet_query}=phd\nOutput:\n{\"facet_filter\":\"DEGREE\",\"facet_values\":[\"PhD\",\"Doctor of Philosophy\",\"Doctorate\",\"Doctoral Degree\"]}\n\nInput: {facet_filter}=DEGREE, {facet_query}=associate\nOutput:\n{\"facet_filter\":\"DEGREE\",\"facet_values\":[\"Associate Degree\",\"AA\",\"AS\",\"Associate of Science\",\"Associate of Arts\"]}\n\n\n\n# --- FIELD_OF_STUDY (covering tech, business, medical, and humanities majors) ---\nInput: {facet_filter}=FIELD_OF_STUDY, {facet_query}=computer science\nOutput:\n{\"facet_filter\":\"FIELD_OF_STUDY\",\"facet_values\":[\"Computer Science\",\"CS\",\"Software Engineering\",\"Information Technology\",\"Informatics\"]}\n\nInput: {facet_filter}=FIELD_OF_STUDY, {facet_query}=finance\nOutput:\n{\"facet_filter\":\"FIELD_OF_STUDY\",\"facet_values\":[\"Finance\",\"Accounting\",\"Economics\",\"Investment Banking\",\"Financial Management\"]}\n\nInput: {facet_filter}=FIELD_OF_STUDY, {facet_query}=nursing\nOutput:\n{\"facet_filter\":\"FIELD_OF_STUDY\",\"facet_values\":[\"Nursing\",\"Healthcare Management\",\"Patient Care\",\"Clinical Nursing\"]}\n\nInput: {facet_filter}=FIELD_OF_STUDY, {facet_query}=psychology\nOutput:\n{\"facet_filter\":\"FIELD_OF_STUDY\",\"facet_values\":[\"Psychology\",\"Behavioral Science\",\"Cognitive Science\",\"Counseling\",\"Human Development\"]}\n\n\n\n# --- SCHOOL (covering US, international, and group-level schools) ---\nInput: {facet_filter}=SCHOOL, {facet_query}=stanford\nOutput:\n{\"facet_filter\":\"SCHOOL\",\"facet_values\":[\"Stanford University\",\"Stanford\",\"Stanford Tech\",\"Stanford GSB\"]}\n\nInput: {facet_filter}=SCHOOL, {facet_query}=uc berkeley\nOutput:\n{\"facet_filter\":\"SCHOOL\",\"facet_values\":[\"UC Berkeley\",\"Berkeley\",\"Cal\",\"UCB\",\"University of California Berkeley\"]}\n\nInput: {facet_filter}=SCHOOL, {facet_query}=ivy league\nOutput:\n{\"facet_filter\":\"SCHOOL\",\"facet_values\":[\"Harvard University\",\"Yale University\",\"Princeton University\",\"University of Pennsylvania\",\"Columbia University\",\"Cornell University\",\"Brown University\",\"Dartmouth College\"]}\n\nInput: {facet_filter}=SCHOOL, {facet_query}=iit\nOutput:\n{\"facet_filter\":\"SCHOOL\",\"facet_values\":[\"IIT Bombay\",\"IIT Delhi\",\"IIT Madras\",\"IIT Kharagpur\",\"IIT Kanpur\"]}\n\n\n\n\n# Skill family\nInput: {facet_filter}=SKILL, {facet_query}=db\nOutput:\n{\"facet_filter\":\"SKILL\",\"facet_values\":[\"SQL\",\"PostgreSQL\",\"MySQL\",\"Oracle Database\",\"MongoDB\",\"Database Design\"]}\n\n# Certification family\nInput: {facet_filter}=CERTIFICATION, {facet_query}=aws sa\nOutput:\n{\"facet_filter\":\"CERTIFICATION\",\"facet_values\":[\"AWS Certified Solutions Architect – Associate\",\"AWS Certified Solutions Architect – Professional\"]}\n\nInput: {facet_filter}=CERTIFICATION, {facet_query}=CFA\nOutput:\n{\"facet_filter\":\"CERTIFICATION\",\"facet_values\":[\"Certiified Financial Accountant\",\"CFA 3\", \"Accounting Expert\"]}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
