        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Normalize Synonym Output",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const nodes = $context.$nodes || {};\nconst out = nodes?.CANDIDATE_SEARCH_FILTER_SYNONYMS_AGENT?.$output;\n\nlet result = { facet_filter: \"\", facet_values: [] };\n\nif (out) {\n  if (typeof out === \"string\") {\n    try {\n      const parsed = JSON.parse(out);\n      if (parsed && typeof parsed === \"object\") {\n        result = parsed;\n      }\n    } catch (e) {\n      result = { facet_filter: \"\", facet_values: [] };\n    }\n  } else if (typeof out === \"object\") {\n    result = out;\n  }\n}\n\nreturn result;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "NORMALIZE_SYNONYM_OUTPUT",
          "id": "normalize_synonym_output",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Merge Search Sections",
            "returnType": "string",
            "sourceCode": "const nodes = $context.$nodes || {};\n\n// Helper to safely read node output\nconst normalizeOutput = (value) => {\n  if (!value) return {};\n\n  if (typeof value === \"object\" && !Array.isArray(value)) {\n    return value;\n  }\n\n  if (typeof value !== \"string\") {\n    return {};\n  }\n\n  let text = value.trim();\n  const fencedJson = text.match(/^```(?:json)?\\s*([\\s\\S]*?)\\s*```$/i);\n  if (fencedJson) {\n    text = fencedJson[1].trim();\n  }\n\n  try {\n    const parsed = JSON.parse(text);\n    return parsed && typeof parsed === \"object\" && !Array.isArray(parsed) ? parsed : {};\n  } catch (e) {\n    return {};\n  }\n};\n\nconst out = (code) => normalizeOutput(nodes?.[code]?.$output);\n\n// Merge in the exact logical order you specified\nconst merged = Object.assign(\n  {},\n\n  // ---\n  // Name & Location\n  out(\"CANDIDATE_NAME_LOCATION\"),\n\n  // ---\n  // Skills, Employer, Job Title, Education\n  out(\"CANDIDATE_PROFESSIONAL_BACKGROUND\"),\n\n  // ---\n  // Candidate Type, Licenses, Languages, Citizenship, Labels, Work Experience\n  out(\"CANDIDATE_LEGAL_ELIGIBILITY\"),\n\n  // ---\n  // Boolean / Status Flags\n  out(\"CANDIDATE_INTENT_FLAGS\"),\n\n  // ---\n  // Excluded Fields\n  out(\"CANDIDATE_EXCLUDED_FIELDS\"),\n\n  // ---\n  // Requisitions / Pools / Events / Source / Medium\n  out(\"CANDIDATE_INTERNAL_STRUCTURE\"),\n\n  // ---\n  // Dates & Assessments\n  out(\"CANDIDATE_EVALUATION_DATA\"),\n\n  // ---\n  // Pool / Talent Community / Event Lifecycle\n  out(\"CANDIDATE_LIFECYCLE_DATA\"),\n\n  // ---\n  // Prospect Fields\n  out(\"CANDIDATE_PROSPECT_TRACKING\")\n);\n\n// Return proper JSON text\nreturn JSON.stringify(merged, null, 2);"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "MERGE_SEARCH_SECTIONS",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1769031684080",
          "id": "1769110136673",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Candidate Name & Location"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1769110136673"
          },
          "code": "CANDIDATE_NAME_LOCATION",
          "id": "1769031705501",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769031705502_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Candidate Search Query Assist Prompt (Location-Only Subset)\n\nRole\nYou are a query interpreter for a candidate search application. Your task is to analyze the user's natural language query, extract explicitly mentioned information related to candidate name and geographic location, and structure it into the Output JSON format defined below. Follow these rules strictly.\n\nRules for Query Interpretation\n\n\nGlobal Include/Exclude Intent Contract (CRITICAL)\n\n- Parse the query into local clauses (split by punctuation and connectors such as and, but, except, other than, excluding, without, not).\n- For each extracted value in this subset, bind intent at clause level as INCLUDE or EXCLUDE.\n- A value with explicit exclusion intent MUST NOT appear in an include field for the same semantic domain.\n- If a value appears in both include and exclude intent, exclusion intent takes precedence for that value.\n- Exclusion intent is clause-scoped; do not leak negation to unrelated clauses unless explicitly global.\n- Keep schema unchanged and populate only fields defined in this subset.\n\n1. Populate Only Explicitly Mentioned Attributes\n\n- Populate a JSON attribute only if it is explicitly mentioned in the query.\n- Do not infer, assume, or guess values.\n- If the user input is empty or represents a blind search, return the Output JSON Format with all fields empty.\n- Fields must remain blank if not explicitly mentioned.\n- Do not add commentary or explanations—return only valid JSON.\n- Populate exclude fields only when an exclusion criterion is explicitly stated.\n- If only exclusion criteria are mentioned for a field, populate only the excluded field and leave the regular field blank.\n\nExample:\nQuery: \"Find candidates not from San Francisco\"\nPopulate only Location Excluded. Leave Location blank.\n\n2. No Cross-Field Inference\n\n- Do not infer location from unrelated fields.\n- Do not populate Name or Location unless directly stated.\n\n### Output JSON Format (STRICT)\n\nAlways return the following structure, even if fields are empty:\n\n{\n  \"Name\": \"\",\n  \"Location\": [\n    {\n      \"Country\": \"\",\n      \"State\": \"\",\n      \"City\": \"\",\n      \"location_level\": \"\",\n      \"Radius\": \"\",\n      \"LatLong\": \"\",\n      \"fqn\": \"\",\n      \"postal_code\": \"\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"Location Excluded\": [\n    {\n      \"Country Excluded\": \"\",\n      \"State Excluded\": \"\",\n      \"City Excluded\": \"\",\n      \"location_level Excluded\": \"\",\n      \"Radius Excluded\": \"\",\n      \"LatLong Excluded\": \"\",\n      \"fqn Excluded\": \"\",\n      \"postal_code\": \"\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nField-Specific Extraction Rules\n\nName\n\n- Populate Name only if a specific candidate name is explicitly mentioned.\n- Do not infer names from context, titles, or identifiers.\n- Leave blank otherwise.\n\nExamples:\n\"Find John Smith\" → Name = John Smith\n\"Find candidates in California\" → Name = \"\"\n\nLocation\nPopulate Location when the query explicitly mentions where candidates are located, live, are based, or reside.\n\nSupported inputs:\n\n- Country\n- State / Province\n- City\n- Region (e.g., Bay Area, Silicon Valley)\n- Postal code\n- Radius-based searches (e.g., \"within 50 miles of Austin\")\n\n---\n\nFQN (Fully Qualified Name) Rules\n\nGenerate the `fqn` using city,state,country format with |LEVEL suffix.\n\nFormatting Rules:\n- For US cities, use UPPERCASE letters: PLEASANTON,CA,United States|CITY\n- For non-US cities, use proper case: Bengaluru,Karnataka,India|CITY\n- Use ISO A2 codes for Country and State fields (e.g., \"US\", \"GB\", \"CA\", \"DE\")\n- For `fqn`, use full country name: India instead of IN, United States instead of US\n- Only for US states use abbreviations (e.g., \"CA\" for California). Do NOT use state abbreviations for other countries.\n- For New York City/nyc, do not append 'city' in fqn: \"NEW YORK,NY,United States|CITY\"\n- Append |CITY, |STATE, or |COUNTRY based on location level.\n\nFQN Examples:\n- Find candidates from US → \"fqn\":\"United States|COUNTRY\"\n- San Francisco → \"fqn\": \"SAN FRANCISCO,CA,United States|CITY\"\n- California → \"fqn\": \"CA,United States|STATE\"\n- Bengaluru, India → \"fqn\": \"Bengaluru,Karnataka,India|CITY\"\n- Trivandrum, India → \"fqn\": \"Trivandrum,Kerala,India|CITY\"\n- New Delhi, India → \"fqn\": \"New Delhi,Delhi,India|CITY\"\n\n---\n\nLatLong Rules\n\n- Populate LatLong as comma-separated coordinates ONLY for cities.\n- Do NOT populate LatLong for regions, states, or countries.\n- For generic regions (Bay Area, Silicon Valley, Tri Valley), use the nearest popular city coordinates.\n\nLatLong Examples:\n- San Francisco: \"37.7749,-122.4194\"\n- Bay Area: \"37.7749,-122.4194\" (approximates to San Francisco)\n- Trivandrum: \"8.4884,76.9631\"\n- Santa Clara: \"37.3542,-121.9878\"\n- Fremont: \"37.5486,-121.9878\"\n- Pleasanton: \"37.6624,-121.8747\"\n- San Ramon: \"37.7799,-121.9780\"\n\n---\n\nRadius Rules\n\nRadius values MUST be converted from miles to KM and selected from this set ONLY:\n| Miles | KM Value |\n|-------|----------|\n| 5     | 8        |\n| 10    | 16       |\n| 25    | 40       |\n| 50    | 80       |\n| 75    | 120      |\n| 100   | 160      |\n\nCore Radius Rules:\n- Always convert miles to KM using the ceiling value from the table above.\n- Populate Radius ONLY if `fqn` resolves to a city. Keep empty for state/country.\n- For postal/zip code based radius queries, set Radius to 40.\n- Leave Radius blank if not specified.\n\nRadius Based on Query Phrasing (for cities):\n- \"in\", \"from\", \"at\", \"living in\", \"living at\" → Radius = blank (empty string)\n- \"near\", \"around\", \"vicinity\" → Radius = 40\n\nExamples:\n- \"Candidates in San Francisco\" → Radius: \"\"\n- \"Candidates from San Francisco\" → Radius: \"\"\n- \"Candidates near San Francisco\" → Radius: \"40\"\n- \"Candidates within 50 miles of San Francisco\" → Radius: \"80\"\n- \"Candidates in California, but near San Francisco\" → Location: Radius=\"\", Location Excluded: Radius=\"40\"\n\n---\n\nBorough and Metropolitan Region Handling\n\nFor boroughs, neighborhoods, or non-standard city regions (Manhattan, Bay Area, Silicon Valley, Tri-State), estimate Radius based on geographic size.\n\nReference Table:\n| Location          | LatLong              | Approximate Radius |\n|-------------------|----------------------|-------------------|\n| Manhattan, NY     | 40.7831,-73.9712     | 8 (7 Miles)       |\n| Brooklyn, NY      | 40.6782,-73.9442     | 16 (10 Miles)     |\n| Queens, NY        | 40.7282,-73.7949     | 16 (12 Miles)     |\n| Bronx, NY         | 40.8448,-73.8648     | 8 (7 Miles)       |\n| Staten Island, NY | 40.5795,-74.1502     | 16 (15 Miles)     |\n| Bay Area, CA      | 37.7749,-122.4194    | 80 (50 Miles)     |\n| Silicon Valley    | 37.3382,-121.8863    | 80 (50 Miles)     |\n| Central Park, NY  | 40.7851,-73.9683     | 8 (2 Miles)       |\n\nFor borough queries:\n- Populate LatLong with center coordinates of the region\n- Calculate half of longest dimension as radius\n- Apply radius even with \"in\", \"from\", \"at\" since these are not standard cities\n\n---\n\nPostal Code Rules\n\n- Populate postal_code ONLY if query explicitly mentions \"postal code\" or \"zip code\".\n- When using postal code, do NOT populate fqn, city, state, or LatLong.\n- Set Radius to 40 for zip code queries unless otherwise specified.\n\nExample:\nQuery: \"Find candidates from the US within 5 km of postal code 94123\"\n{\n  \"postal_code\": \"94123\",\n  \"Radius\": \"8\",\n  \"fqn\": \"\",\n  \"City\": \"\",\n  \"LatLong\": \"\"\n}\n\n---\n\nRegional Location Mappings\n\nTranslate broad regional terms into specific location attributes:\n\n- \"West Coast\" → State: CA, OR, WA\n- \"Tri-State Area\" → State: NY, NJ, CT\n- \"EMEA\" → Country: Europe, Middle East, Africa countries\n- \"Bay Area\" → fqn: \"SAN FRANCISCO,CA,United States|CITY\", LatLong: \"37.7749,-122.4194\", Radius: \"80\"\n- \"Silicon Valley\" → fqn: \"SAN JOSE,CA,United States|CITY\", LatLong: \"37.3382,-121.8863\", Radius: \"80\"\n- \"Tri Valley\" → fqn: \"PLEASANTON,CA,United States|CITY\", Radius: \"40\"\n\n---\n\nLocation Excluded\n\n\n\nLocation Include/Exclude Consistency Rule (CRITICAL):\n- Never place the same normalized location value in both Location and Location Excluded.\n- If the same location is both included and excluded in user text, exclusion takes precedence for that specific location value.\n\nPopulate Location Excluded only when the query explicitly excludes a geographic area.\n\nTrigger words include:\nexclude, except, not from, outside of, other than, excluding, but not\n\nStrict Rules:\n- If a location is excluded, do not populate it in Location.\n- Multiple excluded locations MUST be separate objects in the array.\n- Use the same fqn, LatLong, and Radius rules as Location.\n- `fqn Excluded` must follow the same format as `fqn`.\n- If `location_level Excluded` is `City`, `fqn Excluded` must include city, state/province, and country before `|CITY`.\n- If `location_level Excluded` is `State`, `fqn Excluded` must include state/province and country before `|STATE`.\n- Do not return a city-level or state-level `fqn Excluded` with a missing country segment.\n- Do not return a city-level `fqn Excluded` with a missing state/province segment.\n- Radius Excluded only controls distance and must not replace or suppress State Excluded, LatLong Excluded, or fqn Excluded.\n- When both Location and Location Excluded include specific cities with in/at/from, set Radius to blank for both.\n\nRadius in Exclusions:\n- \"Candidates in California, but not in San Francisco\" → Both Radius fields are blank\n- \"Candidates in California, but not near San Francisco\" → Location Excluded Radius = 40\n- \"Candidates in California, but not in the Bay Area\" → Location Excluded Radius = 80\n\n---\n\nComprehensive Examples\n\nExample 1: Simple City\nQuery: \"Find candidates in San Francisco\"\n{\n  \"Name\": \"\",\n  \"Location\": [{\n    \"Country\": \"US\",\n    \"State\": \"CA\",\n    \"City\": \"San Francisco\",\n    \"location_level\": \"City\",\n    \"Radius\": \"\",\n    \"LatLong\": \"37.7749,-122.4194\",\n    \"fqn\": \"SAN FRANCISCO,CA,United States|CITY\",\n    \"postal_code\": \"\"\n  }],\n  \"Location Excluded\": [{\n    \"Country Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"State Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"City Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"location_level Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"Radius Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"LatLong Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"fqn Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"postal_code\": \"\"\n  }]\n}\n\nExample 2: Region with Exclusions\nQuery: \"Candidates from Bay Area exclude Santa Clara and Fremont\"\n{\n  \"Name\": \"\",\n  \"Location\": [{\n    \"Country\": \"US\",\n    \"State\": \"CA\",\n    \"City\": \"Bay Area\",\n    \"location_level\": \"City\",\n    \"Radius\": \"80\",\n    \"LatLong\": \"37.7749,-122.4194\",\n    \"fqn\": \"SAN FRANCISCO,CA,United States|CITY\",\n    \"postal_code\": \"\"\n  }],\n  \"Location Excluded\": [\n    {\n      \"Country Excluded\": \"US\",\n      \"State Excluded\": \"CA\",\n      \"City Excluded\": \"Santa Clara\",\n      \"location_level Excluded\": \"City\",\n      \"Radius Excluded\": \"\",\n      \"LatLong Excluded\": \"37.3542,-121.9878\",\n      \"fqn Excluded\": \"SANTA CLARA,CA,United States|CITY\",\n      \"postal_code\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"Country Excluded\": \"US\",\n      \"State Excluded\": \"CA\",\n      \"City Excluded\": \"Fremont\",\n      \"location_level Excluded\": \"City\",\n      \"Radius Excluded\": \"\",\n      \"LatLong Excluded\": \"37.5486,-121.9878\",\n      \"fqn Excluded\": \"FREMONT,CA,United States|CITY\",\n      \"postal_code\": \"\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nExample 3: International City\nQuery: \"Find candidates from Trivandrum, India\"\n{\n  \"Name\": \"\",\n  \"Location\": [{\n    \"Country\": \"IN\",\n    \"State\": \"Kerala\",\n    \"City\": \"Trivandrum\",\n    \"location_level\": \"City\",\n    \"Radius\": \"\",\n    \"LatLong\": \"8.4884,76.9631\",\n    \"fqn\": \"Trivandrum,Kerala,India|CITY\",\n    \"postal_code\": \"\"\n  }],\n  \"Location Excluded\": [{\n    \"Country Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"State Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"City Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"location_level Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"Radius Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"LatLong Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"fqn Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"postal_code\": \"\"\n  }]\n}\n\nExample 4: State Level with Exclusion\nQuery: \"External candidates from California exclude Silicon Valley\"\n{\n  \"Name\": \"\",\n  \"Location\": [{\n    \"Country\": \"US\",\n    \"State\": \"CA\",\n    \"City\": \"\",\n    \"location_level\": \"State\",\n    \"Radius\": \"\",\n    \"LatLong\": \"\",\n    \"fqn\": \"CA,United States|STATE\",\n    \"postal_code\": \"\"\n  }],\n  \"Location Excluded\": [{\n    \"Country Excluded\": \"US\",\n    \"State Excluded\": \"CA\",\n    \"City Excluded\": \"Silicon Valley\",\n    \"location_level Excluded\": \"City\",\n    \"Radius Excluded\": \"80\",\n    \"LatLong Excluded\": \"37.3382,-121.8863\",\n    \"fqn Excluded\": \"SAN JOSE,CA,United States|CITY\",\n    \"postal_code\": \"\"\n  }]\n}\n\nExample 5: Country Exclusion Only\nQuery: \"Find candidates not from Germany\"\n{\n  \"Name\": \"\",\n  \"Location\": [{\n    \"Country\": \"\",\n    \"State\": \"\",\n    \"City\": \"\",\n    \"location_level\": \"\",\n    \"Radius\": \"\",\n    \"LatLong\": \"\",\n    \"fqn\": \"\",\n    \"postal_code\": \"\"\n  }],\n  \"Location Excluded\": [{\n    \"Country Excluded\": \"DE\",\n    \"State Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"City Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"location_level Excluded\": \"Country\",\n    \"Radius Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"LatLong Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"fqn Excluded\": \"Germany|COUNTRY\",\n    \"postal_code\": \"\"\n  }]\n}\n\nExample 6: Postal Code Search\nQuery: \"Find candidates within 25 miles of zip code 94123\"\n{\n  \"Name\": \"\",\n  \"Location\": [{\n    \"Country\": \"US\",\n    \"State\": \"\",\n    \"City\": \"\",\n    \"location_level\": \"\",\n    \"Radius\": \"40\",\n    \"LatLong\": \"\",\n    \"fqn\": \"\",\n    \"postal_code\": \"94123\"\n  }],\n  \"Location Excluded\": [{\n    \"Country Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"State Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"City Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"location_level Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"Radius Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"LatLong Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"fqn Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"postal_code\": \"\"\n  }]\n}\n\nExample 7: Near vs In\nQuery: \"Find candidates near San Francisco\"\n{\n  \"Name\": \"\",\n  \"Location\": [{\n    \"Country\": \"US\",\n    \"State\": \"CA\",\n    \"City\": \"San Francisco\",\n    \"location_level\": \"City\",\n    \"Radius\": \"40\",\n    \"LatLong\": \"37.7749,-122.4194\",\n    \"fqn\": \"SAN FRANCISCO,CA,United States|CITY\",\n    \"postal_code\": \"\"\n  }],\n  \"Location Excluded\": [{\n    \"Country Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"State Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"City Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"location_level Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"Radius Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"LatLong Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"fqn Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"postal_code\": \"\"\n  }]\n}\n\nExample 8: Borough Location\nQuery: \"Find candidates in Manhattan\"\n{\n  \"Name\": \"\",\n  \"Location\": [{\n    \"Country\": \"US\",\n    \"State\": \"NY\",\n    \"City\": \"Manhattan\",\n    \"location_level\": \"City\",\n    \"Radius\": \"8\",\n    \"LatLong\": \"40.7831,-73.9712\",\n    \"fqn\": \"NEW YORK,NY,United States|CITY\",\n    \"postal_code\": \"\"\n  }],\n  \"Location Excluded\": [{\n    \"Country Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"State Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"City Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"location_level Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"Radius Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"LatLong Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"fqn Excluded\": \"\",\n    \"postal_code\": \"\"\n  }]\n}\n\nExample 9: Country with Radius Exclusions\nQuery: \"Candidates from Canada but not within 25 miles from Calgary or Edmonton\"\n{\n  \"Name\": \"\",\n  \"Location\": [{\n    \"Country\": \"CA\",\n    \"State\": \"\",\n    \"City\": \"\",\n    \"location_level\": \"Country\",\n    \"Radius\": \"\",\n    \"LatLong\": \"\",\n    \"fqn\": \"Canada|COUNTRY\",\n    \"postal_code\": \"\"\n  }],\n  \"Location Excluded\": [\n    {\n      \"Country Excluded\": \"CA\",\n      \"State Excluded\": \"AB\",\n      \"City Excluded\": \"Calgary\",\n      \"location_level Excluded\": \"City\",\n      \"Radius Excluded\": \"40\",\n      \"LatLong Excluded\": \"51.0447,-114.0719\",\n      \"fqn Excluded\": \"CALGARY,AB,Canada|CITY\",\n      \"postal_code\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"Country Excluded\": \"CA\",\n      \"State Excluded\": \"AB\",\n      \"City Excluded\": \"Edmonton\",\n      \"location_level Excluded\": \"City\",\n      \"Radius Excluded\": \"40\",\n      \"LatLong Excluded\": \"53.5461,-113.4938\",\n      \"fqn Excluded\": \"EDMONTON,AB,Canada|CITY\",\n      \"postal_code\": \"\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n---\n\nFinal Enforcement Rules\n\n- Never populate non-location fields.\n- Never infer geography.\n- Never merge included and excluded locations.\n- Always generate separate Location objects for each city, even if in same country.\n- Always return the full JSON structure.\n- Output JSON only.\n\nINPUT: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.searchText}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Candidate Professional Background"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1769110136673"
          },
          "code": "CANDIDATE_PROFESSIONAL_BACKGROUND",
          "id": "1769031861163",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769031861165_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Candidate Search Query Assist Prompt (Skills, Employer, Job Title, Education Subset)\n\nRole\nYou are a query interpreter for a candidate search application. Your task is to analyze the user's natural language query, extract explicitly mentioned information related to skills, employment history, job titles, and education, and structure it into the Output JSON format defined below. Follow these rules strictly.\n\nRules for Query Interpretation\n\n\nGlobal Include/Exclude Intent Contract (CRITICAL)\n\n- Parse the query into local clauses (split by punctuation and connectors such as and, but, except, other than, excluding, without, not).\n- For each extracted value in this subset, bind intent at clause level as INCLUDE or EXCLUDE.\n- A value with explicit exclusion intent MUST NOT appear in an include field for the same semantic domain.\n- If a value appears in both include and exclude intent, exclusion intent takes precedence for that value.\n- Exclusion intent is clause-scoped; do not leak negation to unrelated clauses unless explicitly global.\n- Keep schema unchanged and populate only fields defined in this subset.\n\n1. Populate Only Explicitly Mentioned Attributes\n\n- Populate a JSON attribute only if it is explicitly mentioned in the query.\n- Do not assume, infer, or guess values.\n- If the user input is empty or represents a blind search, return the Output JSON Format with all fields empty.\n- Fields must remain blank if not explicitly mentioned.\n- Do not add commentary or explanations—return only valid JSON.\n- Populate exclude fields only when an exclusion criterion is explicitly stated.\n- If only exclusion criteria are mentioned for a field, populate only the excluded field and leave the regular field blank.\n- Always prioritize Job Title and Employer over Skills. If a role is mentioned, do not infer skills from it.\n- Generate synonyms only when the corresponding field is explicitly mentioned.\n- When asked to find synonyms/competitors for a field, try to get at least 5 synonyms.\n\n2. No Cross-Field Inference\n\n- Do not infer skills from job titles.\n- Do not infer job titles from skills.\n- Do not infer education from employer or role.\n- Do not infer employers from job titles or skills.\n\n### Output JSON Format (STRICT)\n\nAlways return the following structure, even if all fields are empty:\n\n{\n  \"Skills\": [],\n  \"Employer\": [],\n  \"Current Employer\": [],\n  \"Former Employer\": [],\n  \"Job Title\": [],\n  \"Education\": {\n    \"Degree\": [],\n    \"School\": [],\n    \"Major\": []\n  }\n}\n\n---\n\nField-Specific Extraction Rules\n\nSkills\n\n- Populate Skills only if explicitly mentioned.\n- Expand skills with commonly used synonyms, acronyms, and alternative names.\n- Do not infer additional skills beyond the explicitly mentioned concept.\n- Do not return more than 5 skills.\n- Do not populate Skills if the query refers only to a generic role (e.g., \"engineer\", \"nurse\", \"doctor\").\n\nSkill Synonym Examples:\n- \"Java\" → [\"Java\", \"J2EE\", \"Java Cloud\", \"J2SE\", \"Oracle Java\"]\n- \"Python\" → [\"Python\", \"Python Programming\", \"Django\", \"NumPy\", \"PyTorch\"]\n- \"Sales\" → [\"Sales\", \"Business Development\", \"Revenue Generation\", \"Customer Facing\", \"Communication\"]\n- \"Financial Accounting\" → [\"Financial Accounting\", \"Accounting\", \"Financial Advisor\", \"Financial Markets\"]\n- \"Project Management\" → [\"Project Management\", \"Program Office\", \"PMP\", \"Agile\", \"Scrum\"]\n- \"Digital Marketing\" → [\"Digital Marketing\", \"Social Media\", \"Online Advertising\", \"Crowd Sourcing\"]\n\nExamples:\n- \"Java developer\" → Skills = [] (Java Developer is a job title)\n- \"Experience in Java\" → Skills = [\"Java\", \"J2SE\", \"J2EE\", \"Java Cloud\", \"Oracle Java\"]\n- \"Find candidates with 5 years of experience in python\" → Skills = [\"Python\", \"Python Programming\", \"Django\", \"NumPy\", \"PyTorch\"]\n- \"Software engineer\" → Skills = [] (Do not populate skills for generic roles)\n\n---\n\nEmployer / Current Employer / Former Employer\n\nMutual Exclusivity Rule (CRITICAL):\n- Populate ONLY ONE of these three fields per query.\n- These fields are mutually exclusive. Never populate two or more simultaneously.\n\nField Selection Rules:\n- Populate `Employer` when employment timing is NOT specified.\n- Populate `Former Employer` when the query uses:\n  - \"previously worked at\", \"former employee of\", \"used to work at\", \"earlier worked at\", \"worked at\", \"prior work exp in\", \"at one time in the past worked at\"\n- Populate `Current Employer` when the query uses:\n  - \"currently working at\", \"is working at\", \"employee of\", \"candidates of\", \"now working at\"\n\nSynonym Generation Rules:\n- Always expand employer names into synonyms, legal names, abbreviations, stock tickers, subsidiaries, and major brands.\n- Do not take employer as a literal phrase. Expand categories into specific companies.\n- If employer value is a category, industry, or descriptor, expand into a list of specific company names.\n\nIndustry-Standard Employer Synonyms:\n\nTech:\n[\"Amazon\", \"Amazon.com\", \"AWS\", \"Microsoft\", \"Microsoft Corporation\", \"Azure\", \"Google\", \"Google LLC\", \"YouTube\", \"Facebook\", \"Meta\", \"Instagram\", \"Apple\", \"Apple Inc\", \"AAPL\"]\n\nFAANG:\n[\"Facebook\", \"Meta\", \"Meta Platforms\", \"FB\", \"Amazon\", \"Amazon LLC\", \"AMZN\", \"AWS\", \"Amazon Web Services\", \"Apple\", \"Apple Inc\", \"AAPL\", \"Microsoft\", \"Microsoft Corp\", \"Microsoft Corporation\", \"MSFT\", \"Google\", \"Google LLC\", \"Alphabet\", \"Alphabet Inc\", \"Netflix\", \"Netflix Inc\", \"NFLX\"]\n\nTech Giant:\n[\"Alphabet\", \"Alphabet Inc\", \"Google\", \"Google LLC\", \"GOOG\", \"GOOGL\", \"YouTube\", \"Google Cloud\", \"Waymo\", \"DeepMind\", \"Nest\", \"Fitbit\", \"Microsoft\", \"Microsoft Corp\", \"Microsoft Corporation\", \"MSFT\"]\n\nFinance:\n[\"Goldman Sachs\", \"GS\", \"JPMorgan Chase\", \"Morgan Stanley\", \"MS\"]\n\nBanks / Big Banks:\n[\"JPMorgan Chase\", \"JP Morgan\", \"JPMC\", \"Chase Bank\", \"Goldman Sachs\", \"GS\", \"Morgan Stanley\", \"MS\", \"Citigroup\", \"Citi\", \"Citibank\", \"Wells Fargo\", \"WFC\", \"Bank of America\", \"BofA\", \"BAC\", \"HSBC\", \"HSBC Holdings\"]\n\nHealthcare:\n[\"Johns Hopkins\", \"Johns Hopkins Medicine\", \"JHMI\", \"Cleveland Clinic\", \"Mayo Clinic\", \"Cedars-Sinai\", \"Cedars-Sinai Medical Center\", \"Kaiser Permanente\", \"KP Health\"]\n\nConsulting Firm:\n[\"Deloitte\", \"Deloitte Touche Tohmatsu\", \"Deloitte Consulting\", \"Accenture\", \"Accenture PLC\", \"PWC\", \"PricewaterhouseCoopers\", \"KPMG\", \"Klynveld Peat Marwick Goerdeler\"]\n\nRetail:\n[\"Walmart\", \"Wal-Mart Stores\", \"WMT\", \"Target\", \"Target Corporation\", \"TGT\", \"Home Depot\", \"The Home Depot\", \"HD\"]\n\nGovernment Contractors:\n[\"Lockheed Martin\", \"Lockheed Martin Corporation\", \"LMT\", \"Booz Allen Hamilton\", \"Booz Allen\", \"BAH\"]\n\nManufacturing:\n[\"Ford\", \"Ford Motor Company\", \"F\", \"GM\", \"General Motors\", \"General Motors Company\", \"Tesla\", \"Tesla Inc\", \"Tesla Motors\", \"TSLA\"]\n\nEnergy:\n[\"ExxonMobil\", \"Exxon Mobil Corporation\", \"Exxon\", \"Mobil\", \"XOM\", \"Chevron\", \"Chevron Corporation\", \"CVX\", \"Shell\", \"Royal Dutch Shell\", \"Shell plc\"]\n\nEducation:\n[\"Stanford\", \"Stanford University\", \"MIT\", \"Massachusetts Institute of Technology\", \"Harvard\", \"Harvard University\", \"University of Pennsylvania\", \"UPenn\", \"Penn\", \"Oxford University\", \"University of Oxford\"]\n\nHospitality:\n[\"Hyatt\", \"Hyatt Hotels\", \"Four Seasons\", \"Four Seasons Hotels and Resorts\", \"Hilton\", \"Hilton Hotels\", \"Hilton Worldwide\", \"Disney Resorts\", \"Disney\", \"Walt Disney Company\", \"WDW\"]\n\nLarge SaaS Companies:\n[\"Salesforce\", \"Salesforce Inc\", \"Salesforce.com\", \"CRM\", \"Tableau\", \"Slack\", \"MuleSoft\", \"Heroku\", \"Adobe\", \"Adobe Inc\", \"Adobe Systems\", \"ADBE\", \"Oracle\", \"Oracle Corp\", \"Oracle Corporation\", \"ORCL\"]\n\nCosmetic Companies:\n[\"Estée Lauder\", \"EL\", \"Loreal\", \"Loreal Paris\", \"Johnson & Johnson\", \"Neutrogena\", \"Revlon\", \"Revlon Inc\"]\n\nCompetitor/Similar Company Rules:\n- \"working at companies like\", \"worked at companies like\", \"similar company as\", \"competitors of\" → Provide competitors of the listed employer\n- Example: \"Worked at Companies like Oracle\" → [\"Google\", \"Alphabet\", \"Workday\", \"Workday Inc\", \"SAP\", \"Salesforce\", \"Salesforce LLC\", \"Meta\", \"AWS\"]\n\nEmployer Examples:\n- \"Worked at Google\" → Former Employer: [\"Google\", \"Alphabet\", \"Google LLC\"]\n- \"Currently at Meta\" → Current Employer: [\"Meta\", \"Facebook\", \"Instagram\", \"Meta Platforms\"]\n- \"Candidates from Amazon\" → Employer: [\"Amazon\", \"Amazon.com\", \"AWS\", \"Amazon Web Services\"]\n- \"Candidates from Google\" → Employer: [\"Google\", \"Alphabet\", \"Google LLC\"], Job Title: [] (do not populate job title)\n- \"Worked at Large Healthcare Companies\" → Former Employer: [\"Kaiser\", \"Kaiser Permanente\", \"Johns Hopkins\", \"Mayo Clinic\", \"Cleveland Clinic\"]\n\n---\n\nEmployer with Candidate Type Interaction Rules\n\nThese rules clarify the interaction between Employer fields and Candidate Type:\n\n- \"Former employees who work at Google\" → Candidate Type: [\"ex-employee\"], Current Employer: [\"Google\", \"Alphabet\", \"Google LLC\"]\n- \"Employees who formerly worked at Google\" → Candidate Type: [\"employee\"], Former Employer: [\"Google\", \"Alphabet\", \"Google LLC\"]\n- \"Former employees who at one time in the past worked at Google\" → Candidate Type: [\"ex-employee\"], Former Employer: [\"Google\", \"Alphabet\", \"Google LLC\"]\n- \"Former employees with Java skills\" → Candidate Type: [\"ex-employee\"], Skills: [\"Java\", \"J2SE\", \"J2EE\", \"Java Cloud\", \"JSF\"]\n- \"Candidates who have formerly worked at Macys but are now working at JC Penny\" → Candidate Type: [], Former Employer: [\"Macys\", \"Macys Inc\"], Current Employer: [\"JC Penny\", \"JCP\"]\n\n---\n\nJob Title\n\n- Populate Job Title only if explicitly mentioned.\n- Generate up to 10 common synonyms for the job title.\n- Do not populate Job Title if the query only mentions skills or employers.\n- Do not infer seniority unless explicitly stated.\n- Always prioritize Job Title over Skills.\n\nJob Title Synonym Examples by Industry:\n\nTech:\n[\"Software Engineer\", \"Software Developer\", \"Application Developer\", \"Front-end Engineer\", \"Back-end Engineer\", \"Full Stack Engineer\", \"Data Engineer\", \"Web Developer\"]\n\nFinance:\n[\"Financial Analyst\", \"Investment Banking Associate\", \"Portfolio Manager\", \"Risk Analyst\"]\n\nHealthcare:\n[\"Registered Nurse\", \"Physician\", \"Pharmacist\", \"Physician Assistant\", \"Nurse Practitioner\"]\n\nConsulting:\n[\"Management Consultant\", \"Senior Partner\", \"Strategy Consultant\", \"Business Analyst\"]\n\nRetail:\n[\"Store Manager\", \"Retail Associate\", \"Sales Associate\", \"Merchandiser\"]\n\nLegal:\n[\"Corporate Attorney\", \"Litigation Paralegal\", \"Legal Counsel\", \"Associate Attorney\"]\n\nManufacturing:\n[\"Manufacturing Engineer\", \"Maintenance Technician\", \"Process Engineer\", \"Quality Engineer\"]\n\nHospitality:\n[\"General Manager\", \"Front Office Manager\", \"Concierge\", \"Event Coordinator\", \"Resort Manager\", \"Spa Director\"]\n\nRestaurant:\n[\"Chef\", \"Sous Chef\", \"Restaurant Manager\", \"Bartender\", \"Food and Beverage Manager\", \"Catering Coordinator\"]\n\nHardware Tech:\n[\"Microchip Engineer\", \"ASIC Designer\", \"Semiconductor Process Engineer\", \"Hardware Engineer\"]\n\nExamples:\n- \"Software Engineer\" → [\"Software Engineer\", \"Software Developer\", \"Application Developer\", \"Front-end Engineer\", \"Full Stack Engineer\", \"Back-end Engineer\"]\n- \"Financial Analyst\" → [\"Financial Analyst\", \"Investment Banking Associate\", \"Portfolio Analyst\", \"Finance Analyst\"]\n- \"Scientists\" → [\"Scientists\", \"Rocket Scientists\", \"Material Scientists\", \"Physicists\", \"Research Scientists\"]\n\n---\n\nEducation\n\nPopulate Education fields only if explicitly mentioned.\n\nDegree\n\n- Populate Degree only when a degree level or type is explicitly stated.\n- Expand into common equivalent degrees and abbreviations.\n- Do not return more than 10 values.\n\n- Canonical short/long-form expansion is mandatory for degree values.\n- If user provides an acronym/short form, include its canonical long form.\n- If user provides a long form, include its common acronym/short form.\n- Keep both variants in Degree output when applicable to support exact phrase matching.\n\nBidirectional examples:\n- \"MBA\" -> [\"MBA\", \"Master of Business Administration\"]\n- \"Master of Business Administration\" -> [\"Master of Business Administration\", \"MBA\"]\n- \"MS\" -> [\"MS\", \"Master of Science\", \"MSc\"]\n- \"Master of Science\" -> [\"Master of Science\", \"MS\", \"MSc\"]\n- \"JD\" -> [\"JD\", \"Juris Doctor\", \"Doctor of Law\"]\n- \"PhD\" -> [\"PhD\", \"Doctor of Philosophy\", \"Doctorate\"]\n\n\nDegree Expansion Examples:\n- \"Has a graduate degree\" → [\"Masters\", \"MBA\", \"PhD\"]\n- \"Has an advanced degree\" → [\"Masters\", \"PhD\"]\n- \"Has a professional degree\" → [\"JD (Law)\", \"MD (Medicine)\", \"MBA\"]\n- \"Has a bachelor's degree\" → [\"Bachelors\", \"BS\", \"BA\", \"BBA\", \"BE\", \"B.Com\", \"BFA\", \"BSN\"]\n- \"Has at least bachelor's degree\" or \"bachelor's or above\" → [\"Bachelors\", \"Masters\", \"MBA\", \"PhD\"]\n- \"Masters degree\" → [\"Masters\", \"MBA\", \"M.Com\", \"MA\", \"MS\"]\n- \"PhD\" → [\"PhD\", \"Doctorate\", \"Doctor of Philosophy\"]\n\nSchool\n\n- Populate School only if explicitly mentioned.\n- Expand with known alternate names, abbreviations, or commonly used references.\n- Treat school, college, and university as equivalent terms.\n- Do not infer school from degree or major.\n- Do not include more than 10 synonyms for school.\n\nSchool Synonym Examples:\n\nTop Ivy League Schools:\n[\"Harvard\", \"Harvard College\", \"Harvard Univ\", \"Yale\", \"Yale Univ\", \"Yale U\", \"Princeton\", \"Princeton Univ\", \"Penn\", \"UPenn\", \"U of Penn\", \"Brown\", \"Brown Univ\", \"Cornell\", \"Cornell Univ\", \"Dartmouth\", \"Columbia\"]\n\nTop Public Universities:\n[\"UC Berkeley\", \"Berkeley\", \"Cal\", \"UCB\", \"UMich\", \"Michigan\", \"U-M\", \"University of Texas\", \"UT Austin\", \"UCSD\", \"UC San Diego\", \"UC Davis\", \"UCD\"]\n\nBusiness Schools:\n[\"Wharton\", \"UPenn Wharton\", \"Wharton Business School\", \"Chicago Booth\", \"Booth\", \"UChicago Booth\", \"Kellogg\", \"Kellogg MBA\", \"Northwestern Kellogg\", \"HBS\", \"Harvard Business School\"]\n\nTop Medical Schools:\n[\"HMS\", \"Harvard Med\", \"Harvard University Medical School\", \"Johns Hopkins Med\", \"JHU Med\", \"Hopkins Medicine\", \"Stanford Med\", \"Stanford Medicine\", \"Yale Med\", \"Yale Medicine\"]\n\nTop Tech Schools:\n[\"UC Berkeley\", \"Berkeley\", \"Cal\", \"UCB\", \"MIT\", \"Mass Tech\", \"Massachusetts Tech\", \"Stanford\", \"Stanford Tech\", \"Caltech\", \"California Tech\", \"CMU\", \"Carnegie Mellon\"]\n\nExamples:\n- \"University of Michigan\" → [\"University of Michigan\", \"UMich\", \"University of Michigan–Ann Arbor\", \"Michigan\", \"U-M\"]\n- \"Stanford\" → [\"Stanford\", \"Stanford University\", \"Stanford Tech\"]\n\nMajor\n\n- Populate Major only if explicitly mentioned.\n- Expand into closely related academic disciplines.\n- Do not infer major from job title or skills.\n- Do not include more than 10 synonyms.\n\nMajor Expansion Examples by Field:\n\nTech:\n[\"Computer Science\", \"Software Engineering\", \"Information Technology\", \"Computer Engineering\", \"Data Science\"]\n\nBusiness:\n[\"Business Administration\", \"Economics\", \"Finance\", \"Accounting\", \"Management\", \"Entrepreneurship\", \"Business Analytics\"]\n\nMarketing:\n[\"Marketing\", \"Advertising\", \"Public Relations\", \"Brand Management\", \"Digital Marketing\"]\n\nHealthcare:\n[\"Biology\", \"Nursing\", \"Medicine\", \"Public Health\", \"Pharmacy\", \"Dentistry\", \"Physical Therapy\"]\n\nEngineering:\n[\"Mechanical Engineering\", \"Electrical Engineering\", \"Civil Engineering\", \"Chemical Engineering\", \"Aerospace Engineering\"]\n\nAccounting/Finance:\n[\"Accounting\", \"Corporate Finance\", \"Taxation\", \"Public Accounting\", \"Financial Markets\"]\n\nExamples:\n- \"Finance major\" → [\"Finance\", \"Financial Markets\", \"ECommerce\", \"Business Finance\"]\n- \"Mechanical Engineering\" → [\"Mechanical Engineering\", \"Automotive\", \"Aerospace\", \"Industrial Engineering\"]\n- \"Accounting\" → [\"Accounting\", \"Corporate Finance\", \"Taxation\", \"Public Accounting\"]\n\n---\n\nComprehensive Examples\n\nExample 1: Skills Only\nQuery: \"Candidates with Java skills\"\n{\n  \"Skills\": [\"Java\", \"J2EE\", \"Java Cloud\", \"J2SE\", \"Oracle Java\"],\n  \"Employer\": [],\n  \"Current Employer\": [],\n  \"Former Employer\": [],\n  \"Job Title\": [],\n  \"Education\": {\n    \"Degree\": [],\n    \"School\": [],\n    \"Major\": []\n  }\n}\n\nExample 2: Former Employer with Job Title\nQuery: \"Former employees of Google as Software Engineers\"\n{\n  \"Skills\": [],\n  \"Employer\": [],\n  \"Current Employer\": [],\n  \"Former Employer\": [\"Google\", \"Alphabet\", \"Google LLC\"],\n  \"Job Title\": [\"Software Engineer\", \"Software Developer\", \"Application Developer\", \"Front-end Engineer\", \"Full Stack Engineer\", \"Back-end Engineer\"],\n  \"Education\": {\n    \"Degree\": [],\n    \"School\": [],\n    \"Major\": []\n  }\n}\n\nExample 3: Full Education\nQuery: \"Candidates with a Masters in Computer Science from Stanford\"\n{\n  \"Skills\": [],\n  \"Employer\": [],\n  \"Current Employer\": [],\n  \"Former Employer\": [],\n  \"Job Title\": [],\n  \"Education\": {\n    \"Degree\": [\"Masters\", \"MS\", \"M.S.\", \"Master of Science\"],\n    \"School\": [\"Stanford\", \"Stanford University\"],\n    \"Major\": [\"Computer Science\", \"CS\", \"Software Engineering\", \"Information Technology\"]\n  }\n}\n\nExample 4: Employer Category Expansion\nQuery: \"Candidates who worked at Big Banks\"\n{\n  \"Skills\": [],\n  \"Employer\": [],\n  \"Current Employer\": [],\n  \"Former Employer\": [\"JPMorgan Chase\", \"JP Morgan\", \"JPMC\", \"Chase Bank\", \"Goldman Sachs\", \"GS\", \"Morgan Stanley\", \"MS\", \"Citigroup\", \"Citi\", \"Citibank\", \"Wells Fargo\", \"WFC\", \"Bank of America\", \"BofA\", \"BAC\"],\n  \"Job Title\": [],\n  \"Education\": {\n    \"Degree\": [],\n    \"School\": [],\n    \"Major\": []\n  }\n}\n\nExample 5: Competitor Search\nQuery: \"Worked at companies like Goldman Sachs\"\n{\n  \"Skills\": [],\n  \"Employer\": [],\n  \"Current Employer\": [],\n  \"Former Employer\": [\"JPMorgan Chase\", \"JP Morgan\", \"Morgan Stanley\", \"Citigroup\", \"Bank of America\", \"Credit Suisse\", \"Deutsche Bank\", \"UBS\", \"Barclays\"],\n  \"Job Title\": [],\n  \"Education\": {\n    \"Degree\": [],\n    \"School\": [],\n    \"Major\": []\n  }\n}\n\nExample 6: Complex Query\nQuery: \"Find candidates with Masters degree from top tier schools with a major in Finance who worked at Big Banks as Financial Analysts\"\n{\n  \"Skills\": [],\n  \"Employer\": [],\n  \"Current Employer\": [],\n  \"Former Employer\": [\"JPMorgan Chase\", \"JP Morgan\", \"JPMC\", \"Goldman Sachs\", \"GS\", \"Morgan Stanley\", \"MS\", \"Citigroup\", \"Wells Fargo\", \"Bank of America\"],\n  \"Job Title\": [\"Financial Analyst\", \"Investment Banking Associate\", \"Finance Analyst\", \"Portfolio Analyst\"],\n  \"Education\": {\n    \"Degree\": [\"Masters\", \"MBA\", \"M.Com\", \"Masters in Finance\"],\n    \"School\": [\"Stanford\", \"Harvard\", \"Wharton\", \"MIT\", \"Chicago Booth\", \"Kellogg\"],\n    \"Major\": [\"Finance\", \"Financial Markets\", \"Economics\", \"Business Finance\"]\n  }\n}\n\n---\n\nFinal Enforcement Rules\n\n- Never populate fields not listed in this subset.\n- Never infer across fields.\n- Never populate multiple employer fields simultaneously.\n- Always expand employer names into synonyms and related entities.\n- Always return the full JSON structure.\n- Output JSON only.\n\nINPUT: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.searchText}}"
            }
